  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Answer the following questions.</para>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Use the graph below to pick two points and find the slope between the two points.</para>
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/50c7d9215905030c081ecfbe71d89c5923c2a6ca"/></media></figure></problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The slope of the line is \( - \frac{1}{3} \).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Use your two points in the slope formula to confirm the slope is correct.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. </para>
    <para>\( m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{1-3}{4-(-2)}=\frac{-2}{6}=-\frac{1}{3} \)</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Using the slope and a point, write your equation in point-slope form.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. </para>
    <para>\( m = - \frac{1}{3} \) and \( (4, 1) \)</para>
    <para>\( y - y_1 = m(x - x_1) \) becomes: \( y - 1 = - \frac{1}{3}(x - 4) \).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Now write your equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\( y =- \frac{1}{3} x + \frac{7}{3} \)</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Convert slope-intercept form to standard form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\((x+ 3y)= 7\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
